# HOURLY, AT NO EXTRA SPEND (2026-09-12, principal: "make all openrouter mining n research
# side as frequent as possible for max benefits like hrly if not already").
#
# This ran ONCE A DAY. Twenty-three of every twenty-four hours produced nothing from this seat,
# and a hypothesis never generated is lost permanently -- the preamble's own words.
#
# WHY HOURLY IS FREE RATHER THAN 24x THE BILL. scripts/seats.resolve() already substitutes
# zero-cost models when the paid balance is exhausted, and _free_tier_active() fails TOWARD free.
# FREE TIER ONLY, ON EVERY RUN (principal, 2026-09-12: "make everything free tier on
# openrouter"). The service forces QUANT_FREE_TIER=1 unconditionally, so there is no paid
# hour at all and the monthly bill for this seat is zero by construction rather than by
# a cap that has to hold. Attempts go up 24x against a spend of nothing. A free-tier hunt is worth immeasurably more than no
# hunt, and every finding faces the identical gauntlet either way, so this buys ATTEMPTS and
# never leniency.
[Unit]
# STAGGERED off seat-frontier (2026-08-26). Both seats ran the SAME script under the SAME
# `flock -n` lock, so whichever lost the race exited having done nothing -- a retry slot that
# could never retry. These exist because the original root timer fired into an exhausted quota
# window, and a retry is only a retry if it happens LATER, after the first attempt has resolved
# and (crucially) after the credit pool has had a chance to refill.
Description=Timer for early-window seat: frontier2

[Timer]
OnCalendar=*-*-* *:25:00 UTC
RandomizedDelaySec=180
Persistent=true
Unit=quant-seat-frontier2.service

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
